-- title:
--   A level homomorphism describing the Čerednik–Drinfeld fibres
-- statement:
--   The data are those of the Čerednik–Drinfeld uniformisation of a quaternionic moduli problem, and the conclusion produces a group homomorphism from the arithmetic group $\tilde\Gamma$ (written `Γt`) to the level-twisting group $G$, together with four compatibility statements for the formal family `Θf`.
--
--   **Numerical data.** Primes $r$, $\bar r$ and a non-zero natural number $N$, with `hrr` : $\bar r\neq r$, `hrN` : $r\nmid N$, `hrbarN` : $\bar r\nmid N$ and `hN` : $N$ squarefree.
--
--   **Base rings.** A characteristic-zero domain $\mathcal O$ which is a discrete valuation ring (`hdvr`), an irreducible element $\pi$ (`hπ`), completeness of $\mathcal O$ for the $\pi$-adic topology (`hcomplete`), residue ring of cardinality $r$ (`hres`), and $(r)=(\pi)$ as ideals of $\mathcal O$ (`hunr`); a characteristic-zero field $K_0$ which is a fraction field of $\mathcal O$. Further, a characteristic-zero domain $Onr$ over $\mathcal O$ with an $\mathcal O$-algebra automorphism $Fr$, subject to: $\pi$-adic completeness (`hOnr_complete`), maximality of $(\pi)$ in $Onr$ (`hOnr_max`), every element satisfying a monic $\mathcal O$-polynomial modulo $\pi$ (`hOnr_alg`), every monic polynomial of positive degree having a root modulo $\pi$ (`hOnr_closed`), and $Fr(x)\equiv x^{r}\pmod\pi$ (`hFr`). A monoid homomorphism `vdet` from $\mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$ to $\mathbb Z$ written multiplicatively, characterised by `hvdet`: $\mathrm{vdet}(g)=n$ if and only if $\det g=u\pi^{n}$ for some $u\in\mathcal O^{\times}$.
--
--   **The indefinite side and the moduli schemes.** Rationals $a,b$ with `hB` : the quaternion algebra $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a,b]$ satisfies $0<a$ or $0<b$ and is a division algebra at exactly those finite places dividing $r$ or $\bar r$; a maximal order $\Lambda$ (`hΛ`). A scheme $\mathcal X$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$ with a functorial assignment `pt` of points to fake elliptic curves (abelian surfaces with $\Lambda$-action and level-$N$ structure in the sense of the structure `FakeEllipticCurve`), which is a coarse moduli space (`h𝒳`, five clauses: invariance under isomorphism, compatibility with pullback, bijectivity on geometric points over algebraically closed fields, and the universal property). An integer $n$ with $n\ge 3$, $r\nmid n$, $\bar r\nmid n$ and $\gcd(n,N)=1$; a scheme $M$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$ with `ptF` a fine moduli family for curves with full level-$n$ structure (`hM`, four clauses). A group $G$ with $\rho:G\to\operatorname{Aut}M$ and $\chi:G\to\Lambda$ such that `hρ` holds: each $\rho(g)$ lies over the base, $\rho(g)$ implements the twist of the level-$n$ structure by $\chi(g)$, and $\chi$ is multiplicative, injective and surjective modulo $n$. A morphism $p:M\to\mathcal X$ over the base (`hp`), invariant under $\rho$ (`hρp`), forgetting the level structure on points (`hp_pt`).
--
--   **Hecke tower and Atkin–Lehner data.** For each prime $\ell\notin\{r,\bar r\}$ a scheme $\mathcal Y_\ell$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$ with a coarse moduli family `ptT` for curves with an extra level-$\ell$ structure (`h𝒴`), and two degeneracy morphisms $d_0,d_1:\mathcal Y_\ell\to\mathcal X$ over the base (`hd₀f`, `hd₁f`) which on points forget the extra level structure (`hd₀`) and pass to an $\ell$-isogenous quotient (`hd₁`). Endomorphisms $a_r$, $a_{\bar r}$ of $\mathcal X$ over the base (`harf`, `harbarf`) realising the Atkin–Lehner quotients at $r$ and at $\bar r$ on points (`har`, `harbar`).
--
--   **The definite side.** Rationals $a_1,b_1$ with `hdef`: $a_1<0$, $b_1<0$ and $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a_1,b_1]$ a division algebra at exactly the places dividing $\bar r$; a maximal order $\Lambda_1$, an Eichler order $R_1$ of level $N$, with $R_1\le\Lambda_1$; an adelic unit $n_1$ in the prime Hecke set of $R_1$ at $r$ (`hn₁`) such that $R_1\cap n_1R_1n_1^{-1}$ is an Eichler order of level $Nr$ (`hS₁`); an injective $\mathbb Q$-algebra embedding $\iota_0$ of $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a_1,b_1]$ into $M_2(K_0)$; a height-one prime $v$ of $\mathbb Z$ containing $r$. The subgroup $\tilde\Gamma$ is characterised by `hΓt` as the group of quaternion units lying, at every finite place $w\neq v$, in the subgroup generated by the local unit box of $R_1$ at $w$. Families $s_\ell$ of quaternion units and $s^{f}_\ell$ of adelic units for $\ell\notin\{r,\bar r\}$, with `hs` (four clauses): the component of $s^{f}_\ell$ at a place not containing $r$ is $s_\ell\otimes 1$, its component at a place containing $r$ is $1$, the product of the diagonal image of $\ell$ with $(s^{f}_\ell)^{-1}$ lies in the level Hecke set of $\Lambda_1$ and $R_1\cap n_1R_1n_1^{-1}$ at $\ell$ when $\ell\mid N$ and in the prime Hecke set of that intersection otherwise, and $\mathrm{nrd}(s_\ell)=\ell$; the groups $\tilde\Gamma_\ell=\tilde\Gamma\cap s_\ell\tilde\Gamma s_\ell^{-1}$ (`hΓtℓ`). A unit $\bar w$ of reduced norm $\bar r$ normalising $\tilde\Gamma$ (`hwbar`). Also `hΛℤ`: every integer lies in $\Lambda$, and a coordinate map `coord` from $\Lambda$ to pairs of Witt vectors over the quadratic Galois field of characteristic $r$, satisfying `hcoord` (additive, unital, multiplicative with a Frobenius twist, injective, with dense image and the prescribed trace identity).
--
--   **The special-fibre package** over the residue ring $k_0=Onr/\pi$: a fake elliptic curve $A_0$, a formal $\mathcal O_D$-module $X_0$ of dimension $2$ with an action of the unramified quadratic ring and a uniformiser endomorphism, formal coordinates $\theta_0$ of dimension $2$ on $A_0$, endomorphism families $e,e':\tilde\Gamma\to\operatorname{End}(A_0)$ with $e_\gamma$ over the base (`he`) and degrees `deg`; `hX₀` : $X_0$ has height $4$; `hA₀` : $A_0$ is a formal module via `coord`, $X_0$, $\theta_0$. The conditions on these (summarised here) are: `hE1`, each pair $(e_\gamma,e'_\gamma)$ is an isogeny pair of degree $r^{\deg\gamma}$ preserving the level-$N$ structure; `hE1mul`, multiplicativity of $\gamma\mapsto e_\gamma$ up to multiplication by powers of $r$; `hE1sc`, for rational-integral scalars $\gamma=c$ the endomorphism $e_\gamma$ is the action of $c$ up to powers of $r$; `hE1'`, conversely, if $e_\gamma$ becomes the action of a positive integer after multiplying by a power of $r$ then $\gamma$ is a rational scalar; `hE2`, for every injective ring homomorphism from the centraliser of the $X_0$-action and its uniformiser endomorphism into $M_2(K_0)$ there is $g\in\mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$ such that each $e_\gamma$ is induced on formal coordinates by an element $\varepsilon$ of that centraliser whose image is $r^{k_\gamma}\,g\,\iota_0(\gamma)\,g^{-1}$; `hE3`, for every full level-$n$ structure on $A_0$ there are labels $\mathrm{lab}:\tilde\Gamma\to\Lambda$ describing the action of $e_\gamma$ on that structure, multiplicative modulo $n$ and matching scalars modulo $n$; `hE4`, over algebraically closed fields every $r$-power isogeny self-map preserving the level structure on a pullback of $A_0$ arises from some $e_\gamma$ up to powers of $r$. Finally an order $R_2\le R_1$ (`hR₂`, `hR₂o`) such that every element of $R_1$ becomes an element of $R_2$ after multiplication by a power of $r$ (`hR₂r`), together with $\hat e:R_2\to\operatorname{End}(A_0)$ over the base (`hê`) and the clauses `hE5a` (additivity on points, commutation with the $\Lambda$-action, preservation of level), `hE5b1`–`hE5b3` (unitality, multiplicativity, integers), `hE5c` ($\hat e(\bar x)\circ\hat e(x)$ is the action of $\mathrm{nrd}(x)$), `hE5d` (compatibility of $\hat e$ with $e_\gamma$ when $x=r^{k}\gamma$), and `hE5e` (a joint matrix realisation as in `hE2` for $\tilde\Gamma$ and for $R_2$ simultaneously).
--
--   **The Drinfeld-side package.** A ring homomorphism $\iota$ from the unramified quadratic ring to $Onr$; a formal $\mathcal O_D$-module $\Phi$ over $Onr/(r)$ which is special for the structure map induced by $\iota$ (`hΦ`) and of height $4$ (`hΦ4`); a moduli package $MD$ over $Onr$ satisfying the Zariski sheaf condition (`hMD`); a family $\eta$ assigning to each rigidified object over a ring $B$ with $r$ nilpotent a point of $MD$, subject to `hη` (three clauses: on admissible objects over Noetherian rings $\eta$ separates precisely isomorphism classes; $\eta$ is compatible with base change; every point of $MD$ is, on a Zariski cover by localisations, the image under $\eta$ of an admissible rigidified object). An injective ring homomorphism $E_0$ from the centraliser of the $\Phi$-action and its uniformiser endomorphism into $M_2(K_0)$ whose image is commensurable with $M_2(\mathcal O)$ in the precise two-sided sense of `hE₀`. A natural transformation `eD` from the functor of $G$-points of $MD$ over $\mathcal O$ to the product of the functor corepresented by $Onr$ with Deligne's functor $\Omega$ of lines in lattice base changes, with `hnatD` (naturality), `hbijD` (bijectivity on every Noetherian $\mathcal O$-algebra in which $\pi$ is nilpotent), `hfstD` (the first component is the structure map $\psi$), `hGLD` (the action of $g\in\mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$ on $MD$-points corresponds to the twisted action in which the leg is composed with $Fr^{-\mathrm{vdet}(g)}$ and the Deligne datum is pulled back along $g^{-1}$), `hPiD` and `hPiexD` ($\pi$-translation corresponds to a single Frobenius twist of the leg, and $\pi$-translates exist). Moreover a ring homomorphism $\kappa$ from $Onr/\pi$ to $Onr/(r)$ compatible with the quotient maps (`hκ`), a natural number $n_0$ and a series $\beta_0$ which is an isogeny of formal $\mathcal O_D$-modules from $\Phi$ to the base change of $X_0$ along $\kappa$, of height $4n_0$ (`hβ₀`).
--
--   **Level structure and the Atkin–Lehner datum at $\bar r$ on $A_0$.** A full level-$n$ structure $P_0$ on $A_0$; a fake elliptic curve $A_{0w}$ with morphisms $aw$, $aw'$ exhibiting it as the Atkin–Lehner quotient of $A_0$ at $\bar r$ (`hALw`), morphisms $bw$, $bw'$ forming an isogeny pair of degree $r^{k_w}$ between $A_{0w}$ and $A_0$ (`hBSw`) with $bw$ preserving level (`hBSwlev`), the compatibilities `haw`, `haw'`, `hbw`, `habw`, and `hJOINTw`: for every injective ring homomorphism from the centraliser into $M_2(K_0)$ there is a single $g$ realising all the $e_\gamma$ as in `hE2` and, in addition, realising the composite $aw$ followed by $bw$ by an element whose image is $r^{k_w}\,g\,\iota_0(\bar w)\,g^{-1}$.
--
--   **The comparison map $\Xi$ and the family $\Theta_f$.** A map $\Xi$ sending a rigidified curve over a Noetherian $\mathcal O$-algebra $B$ with $\pi$ nilpotent (a fake elliptic curve $E$ together with a rigidification: a reduction $E_b$ of $E$ modulo $\pi$, a pullback $A_b$ of $A_0$ along the residue leg, and an $r$-power isogeny $E_b\to A_b$ preserving level) to a $G$-point of $MD$, subject to: `hΞleg` (over connected $B$ the leg of $\Xi x$ is a Frobenius twist of $\psi$), `hΞnat` (naturality under pullbacks of curves and rigidifications), `hΞiso` (invariance under isomorphisms of rigidified curves possessing the displayed comparison data), and `hΞdef` (over connected $B$ with $r$ nilpotent, a curve carrying a formal module structure via `coord` has $\Xi$ computed by $\eta$ applied to an admissible rigidified object $t$ with $t.X=X$ obtained by rigidified transport through $\theta_0,\kappa,\beta_0$ with a shift $j\le 1$, the leg being twisted by $Fr^{-j}$). An element $g_0\in\mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$, and the two equivariance hypotheses `heqΓ` (translating a rigidification by $e_\gamma$ moves the $MD$-point by the action of $r^{c}\,g_0\,\iota_0(\gamma)\,g_0^{-1}$ for some $c\in\mathbb Z$) and `heqW` (the analogous statement for an Atkin–Lehner quotient at $\bar r$ with $\bar w$ in place of $\gamma$, under invertibility of $\bar r$ in $B$). The four hypotheses `hK1`–`hK4` express that, after the twist by $g_0^{-1}$, the assignment $(E,\varrho)\mapsto \mathrm{eD}(\Xi(E,\varrho))$ hits every pair $(\psi,P)$ over connected bases (`hK1`), does so uniquely up to an isomorphism of curves with compatible comparison data (`hK2`), is compatible with base change along $\mathcal O$-algebra maps (`hK3`), and lifts along surjections with square-zero kernel in the stated sense (`hK4`). The normalised level transport is supplied by `hC0e` (existence of a full level-$n$ structure transported from $P_0$ through a rigidification, for curves with a formal module structure over connected bases) and `hC0u` (uniqueness of its underlying point). Finally $\Theta_f$ assigns to every Noetherian $\mathcal O$-algebra $B$ with $\pi$ nilpotent and every triple consisting of a leg $\psi:Onr\to B$, a Deligne datum $P$ and an element of $G$ a morphism $\operatorname{Spec}B\to M$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$, subject to `hnat` (naturality in $B$), `hG` (composing with $\rho(h)$ replaces the $G$-coordinate $g\cdot h$ by $g$), `hC2` (the morphism attached to $((\psi,P),1)$ is the fine-moduli point of $(E,P_n)$ whenever $(E,\varrho)$ has $\Xi$-leg the $g_0$-twist of $\psi$, corresponds to $(\psi,P)$ under the $g_0^{-1}$-twisted action, and $P_n$ is a normalised level transport) and `hC2c` (the same morphism followed by $p$ is the coarse-moduli point of $E$).
--
--   **Conclusion.** There exists a group homomorphism $\tilde\theta:\tilde\Gamma\to G$ with the following four properties.
--
--   (1) *Equivariance of $\Theta_f$.* For every Noetherian $\mathcal O$-algebra $B$ with $\pi$ nilpotent, every unit $\gamma$ of $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a_1,b_1]$ lying in $\tilde\Gamma$, all pairs $x,x'$ consisting of a leg and a Deligne datum over $B$, and all $g\in G$: if $x'$ is obtained from $x$ by the twisted action of $\iota_0(\gamma)$, that is, the leg of $x'$ is the leg of $x$ composed with $Fr^{-\mathrm{vdet}(\iota_0\gamma)}$ and the datum of $x'$ is the pullback of that of $x$ along $\iota_0(\gamma)^{-1}$, then $\Theta_f(x',\tilde\theta(\gamma)g)=\Theta_f(x,g)$.
--
--   (2) *Fibres over algebraically closed fields.* For every algebraically closed field $k$ which is an $\mathcal O$-algebra with $\pi$ nilpotent, all legs $\psi,\psi':Onr\to k$, all Deligne data $P,P'$ over $k$ and all $g,g'\in G$, the equality $\Theta_f((\psi,P),g)=\Theta_f((\psi',P'),g')$ holds if and only if there is $\gamma\in\tilde\Gamma$ such that $g'=\tilde\theta(\gamma)g$, such that $P'$ is the pullback of $P$ along $\iota_0(\gamma)^{-1}$, and such that for every $y\in Onr$ fixed by $Fr^{\mathrm{vdet}(\iota_0 z)}$ for all rational scalars $z\in\tilde\Gamma$ with $\tilde\theta(z)=1$, one has $\psi'(y)=\psi(Fr^{-\mathrm{vdet}(\iota_0\gamma)}y)$.
--
--   (3) *Translation of rigidifications on a fixed curve.* For every Noetherian $\mathcal O$-algebra $B$ with $\pi$ nilpotent and without non-trivial idempotents, every leg $\psi$, Deligne datum $P$, fake elliptic curve $E$ over $B$ and rigidification $\varrho$ of $E$ relative to the $g_0$-twisted leg, such that the leg of $\Xi(E,\varrho)$ is that twist and $\mathrm{eD}(\Xi(E,\varrho))$ corresponds to $(\psi,P)$ under the $g_0^{-1}$-twisted action: for every $\gamma\in\tilde\Gamma$ and every pair $(\psi',P')$ obtained from $(\psi,P)$ by the twisted action of $\iota_0(\gamma)$ there exists a rigidification $\varrho'$ of the *same* curve $E$ relative to the $g_0$-twist of $\psi'$ such that: the leg of $\Xi(E,\varrho')$ is that twist; $\mathrm{eD}(\Xi(E,\varrho'))$ corresponds to $(\psi',P')$ under the $g_0^{-1}$-twisted action; for any normalised level transports $P_n$ through $\varrho$ and $P_n'$ through $\varrho'$ of $P_0$, the point of $P_n'$ is the image of the point of $P_n$ under the action of $\chi(\tilde\theta(\gamma))$ on $E$; and for every prime $\ell\neq r$ invertible in $B$, every extra level-$\ell$ structure on $A_0$ (named `K₀` in the statement, shadowing the fraction field) that is preserved by $e_\gamma$, and any extra level-$\ell$ structures $C$, $C'$ on $E$ which are carried into it through $\varrho$ and through $\varrho'$ respectively, the subschemes $C$ and $C'$ define the same notion of a point of $E$ factoring through them.
--
--   (4) *Isomorphisms of curves over algebraically closed fields.* For every algebraically closed field $k$ which is an $\mathcal O$-algebra with $\pi$ nilpotent, every leg $\psi$, Deligne data $P,P'$, curves $E,E'$ over $k$ with rigidifications $\varrho$, $\varrho'$ relative to the $g_0$-twist of $\psi$ whose $\Xi$-legs are that twist and whose images under $\mathrm{eD}\circ\Xi$ correspond to $(\psi,P)$ and $(\psi,P')$ respectively under the $g_0^{-1}$-twisted action, and every isomorphism $i:E\to E'$ over $k$ compatible with the group laws, the $\Lambda$-actions and the level-$N$ structures: there exists $\gamma\in\tilde\Gamma$ such that $(\psi,P')$ is obtained from $(\psi,P)$ by the twisted action of $\iota_0(\gamma)$; for any normalised level transports $P_n$ through $\varrho$ and $P_n'$ through $\varrho'$ of $P_0$, the morphism $i$ carries the $\chi(\tilde\theta(\gamma))$-twist of the point of $P_n$ to the point of $P_n'$; and for every prime $\ell\neq r$ invertible in $k$, every extra level-$\ell$ structure on $A_0$ and extra level-$\ell$ structures $C$ on $E$, $C'$ on $E'$ carried into it through $\varrho$ and $\varrho'$ respectively, the statement that $i$ identifies $C$ with $C'$ (points of $E$ factor through $C$ exactly when their images under $i$ factor through $C'$) is equivalent to the statement that $e_\gamma$ preserves the chosen extra level-$\ell$ structure on $A_0$.
--
--   This is the step of the Čerednik–Drinfeld uniformisation at which the arithmetic group $\tilde\Gamma$ of units of the definite quaternion algebra, integral away from the place above $r$, is mapped into the group $G$ twisting full level-$n$ structures, and the fibres of the formal family $\Theta_f$ over the product of the unramified leg with Deligne's functor of lines are identified with $\tilde\Gamma$-orbits, curve-theoretically as well as on points. It feeds the construction of the Čerednik–Drinfeld family in [`CerednikDrinfeld.QM.IsFineModuli.exists_cerednikDrinfeld_fineFamily_of_rigidifiedToG_of_isNoetherianRing_heightNormalised_eq_oneLegC5_h2`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.QM.IsFineModuli.exists_cerednikDrinfeld_fineFamily_of_rigidifiedToG_of_isNoetherianRing_heightNormalised_eq_oneLegC5_h2).
